Future Trunks flashing onto the scene  out of nowhere taking out the most  prolific villain in Dragonball history  soon becoming one of the most popular  characters in the entire series however  with a saga that includes moments such  as this I often felt as though a  particular relationship dynamic was  largely kept out of the spotlight so as  I often do I decided to go to my Twitter  to ask my followers what they thought  asking the question which of these was  your favorite relationship in Dragon  Balls sellar I provided three options to  choose from and with over two thousand  votes cast the clear winner was Gohan  and Goku and while I think there are  definitely a lot of aspects to love  about the relationship and interactions  during this part of the story today I  want to bring attention to and focus on  or I believe is one of the most  underrated fantastic and believable  relationships ever told in Dragonball I  want to take an in-depth look at how  trunks and his scenes were written to  achieve an emotional connection with the  audience to explore how the supporting  characters played a role in reinforcing  this relationship and to explain how a  father and son dynamic builds one of the  most realistic and cathartic  relationships in the show's history this  is Future Trunks the wounded  [Music]  in storytelling what makes a character  and story interesting is largely the  conflict according to km ones book  creating character arcs there are four  aspects that make up the arc and the  conflict in a character's mind these are  the lie that they believe the thing they  want the thing they need and the wound  to begin our dissection of trunks is  character I think it's important we  first understand the storytelling term  wound  according to author km Wyland wound is  movie speak for something in your  character's past that haunts him often  the wound will be something shocking and  traumatic this wound from a traumatic  event typically causes or is connected  to the live the character believes which  is the harboring of some deeply held  misconception the character either  believes about themselves the world or  both  in other words the characters wound  often goes hand in hand with the lie  that they believe and need to overcome  over the course of the story for example  in the case of Marvel's spider-man  homecoming Peters wound is his Uncle  Ben's murder it's something he blames  himself for something that drives him  throughout the stories one time and  continues to do so today at the same  time the lie that he believes is that he  needs the suit to be spider-man that in  order to be a hero he needs that special  suit Tony Stark provided for him to  which Tony Stark responds if you're  nothing without this shoe then you  shouldn't have it okay in this one scene  Peter desire to help others is  demonstrated his wound Uncle Ben's death  motivating him but at the same time it's  made evident through his own words that  he doesn't fully believe in himself  which is the lie his character beliefs  in the case of trunks during his  unveiling he comes off as a confident  and capable fighter breezing through the  largest foe the series has seen in an  instant with a smirk on his face  however shortly after we soon find out  that he isn't as sure-footed as he  initially appeared we eventually learned  that trunks comes from an alternate  future where everyone but himself  Bulma and a few others have died the  individuals responsible the androids  Despicable cyborgs responsible for  taking trunks his only father figure  away from him Gohan  this is trunks is wound trunks blames  himself for Gohan's death and his  timeline if he had been stronger if he  had been better maybe he could have  saved him  as a result of this trauma the light  trunks now believes is that he needs  someone else to save his timeline for  him he needs help  additionally he deeply desires to meet  and build a relationship of some form  with the father he never had a chance to  meet which leads me nicely into what I  believe was trunks his most important  play in the series his interactions with  a certain character Samara Damiano the  Cheetahs wound or traumatic  life-changing event was his planets  destruction and his upbringing under  Frieza he was raised to believe that  strength was all that mattered and that  he was destined to be the strongest  Saiyan  however when he finds out that that  isn't the case suddenly becoming  stronger and demonstrating his  superiority becomes the only thing that  occupies his mind Vegeta now thinks that  the only thing worth pursuing his power  that is the lie that Vegeta believes and  he puts up a strong guard against those  that suggest otherwise however in trunks  his first conversation with Goku before  leaving to the past he comments that  Vegeta looks lonely  forms Goku that that was what made Bulma  interact with him in the first place  she had sympathy for Vegeta but that's  not to say trunks is perfect either this  is the terrific example of character  values in conflict in John troubies book  the anatomy of story he writes identify  a set of values for your hero and each  of the other main characters make each  set of values as different from the  others as possible as your hero and his  opponents fight over the goal make sure  their values come into direct conflict  in other words establish the theme of  your story set the main goal for all the  characters to aim for and give all the  characters pushing towards that goal  different values in the case of trunks  and Vegeta in this instance they are  working towards the same goal but have  vastly different ideas of what they  think it takes to achieve that goal when  the androids are woken up trunks  unleashes a massive blast without  warning after which Vegeta remarks that  that was an entirely pointless effort  which it was trunks believes that the  androids are too monstrous and that they  shouldn't even try he's ruled by fear  and vengeance clouding his judgment  leading to poor decisions being made  Vegeta on the other side of the coin  thinks that nothing can be greater than  he is and that if they are that strong  he should still be the one to face them  anyway these actions are motivated by  the wounds both characters have endured  in their pasts resulting in them both  living out the lies that they hold to be  true trunks ruled by fear of loss and  destruction deems it impossible to win  without help and Vegeta believing only  he can do it refusing any help however  something happens during Vegeta's fight  with 18 trunks remarks I never knew my  father was so powerful he's holding his  own against those androids androids we  later find out are tougher than those in  trunks his timeline trunks  underestimates what he and others are  capable of because of his fear and  experiences however by that same token  Vegeta overestimates what he is capable  of casting aside the notion of ever  working as part of a team it's worth  mentioning at this point that trunks was  correct in his estimations of the  Android  that alone Vegeta was no match for a  teen once his stamina was drained  however his estimation of what a Saiyan  as capable of was skewed by fear and  when faced with another father figure  down one arm on the brink of death  trunks acts on emotion making matters  worse by including Android 17 trunks is  naive but he doesn't know it yet  Vegeta makes a lot of mistakes but he  never makes the mistake of under  estimating what he is capable of as  mentioned by both piccolo and Goku in  this arc Vegeta is a fighting genius  demonstrating a mental toughness and  resilience that trunks is sorely lacking  perfectly shown by their first reactions  to the inside of the time chamber with  trunks distraught and Vegeta delighted  due to the trauma of trunks is past and  his belief that he needs help to succeed  he can't clearly take stock of what he  is capable of when that is all that  Vegeta can see clearly above himself now  locked in a room together Vegeta is  forced to share a space with his son and  trunks is forced to challenge his limits  in ways he never thought possible the  lies they tell themselves are almost  perfect opposites trunks wants group  cooperation but doesn't believe it  himself Vegeta believes only in himself  and wants nothing to do with teamwork  both of their lives are in direct  conflict and as a result they force each  other to change  [Music]  the positive change arc sees the  protagonist start out with varying  degrees of denial and suffering as the  story progresses he's forced to  challenge his beliefs above both himself  and the world around him until finally  overcoming these inner demons changing  for the better  Vegeta realizes in this moment that he  does care about other people he cares  about his son  despite being uncaring and unkind to the  Past he dashes in to avenge his son in  the same careless manner trunks stood  against Android 18 this was not a smart  move  when Vegeta apologizes for moments later  however to complete his arc for this  saga he works as part of a team to  defeat cell alongside Gohan playing the  supporting role thanks to trunks Vegeta  whether he wants to admit it now or not  cares that has grown as a character for  the better  trunks woods revived after all his  experience through his time with the  main cast has overcome his internal  struggle - he now believes that he has  what it takes to protect his future  again this is similar to the plot of  spider-man homecoming as Peter is seen  being crushed beneath a large and very  heavy object he cries out for help but  no one answers through his struggles in  the film he realizes that the help Tony  gave him didn't make him spider-man he  is and always has been  spider-man and people are depending on a  Peter rising to the occasion utilizing  his wound as a motivation to overcome  his lie results in one of the most  moving and inspirational moments of the  film in that same wave Vegeta and the  rest of the supporting cast helped  motivate and improve trunks to the point  where he no longer needs help he can  take care of his world alone he always  had that ability or potential in him he  just couldn't see it he is no longer a  boy he is now a man there are tons of  famous father and son stories in fiction  where both characters address their  shortcomings and ultimately challenge  each other to be better in ways they  would never have been able to do alone  having given myself the time to reflect  upon the story that was told between  these two characters through this lens I  now see and better understand how  important this aspect of the narrative  was in creating the moments we all loved  and appreciated on the sir  thanks to the addition of trunks the  past traumas of both himself and Vegeta  were exposed and challenged for the  better ultimately forcing each other to  heal from their past traumas to  relinquish their lies they believed and  to adopt a new truth moving forward this  relationship is a complex tale full of  innocence hope pride and ultimately  catharsis and it's thanks to this father  and sons story we've learned that in  order to heal you need to call attention  to and address the wounded characters  thanks for watching  you
 

